Z||000011||California Kid||08-09-2001||08:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by COUNTIBLIS:<BR><B>ok,  whos yellow gt is that and where can i find those rims and that side sticker on the fender wheel?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It's Mine! The rims are OZ Monte Carlo with Carbon Fiber Centers 16 X 7 1/2 offset 5 3/8 inch, Part Number 23032202. Car is lowered 1 1/2 inch front and rear.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Post_Fender_Badge.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Post_Engine_1.jpg"> <BR>I contracted Paul McKibben on the internet to make the Fender Badge for me, supplied sketches of what I wanted, and worked it out via e-mail. Paul is great to work with, you can reach him at fierosails@yahoo.com<P>||||reg||6
Z||000012||jelly2m8||08-09-2001||09:12 PM||||&gt;&gt;   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR><B>&gt;&gt;&gt;Man, I love this car.  I think the color is awesome and that decklid scoop is killer!  Who's car is this anyway?  Is it yours Raydar?&lt;&lt;&lt;<BR>.............................................<BR> This car is owned by Wade Custance, Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada.<P> It is a '86 SE with a 350 hp, 350 sbc. 4 spd trans. This thing works as well as it looks, and sounds even sweeter than any other V8 Fiero i've seen, with the 4 supertrapps.<P> I have some video footage of Wade leaving my place, and stomping on the gas. now only if i had a video in card!!!, maybe someday I can get it on the web.<P> This is the car that told me I needed a V8 too. I was one of the non-believers , thinking hopped up V6's can cut it, they DONT!.<BR> One drive in that car, and I had my own 6 months later............<BR>  <P>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 08-09-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Slammed Fiero||08-09-2001||09:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by COUNTIBLIS:<BR>[b]ok,  whos yellow gt is that and where can i find those rims and that side sticker on the fender wheel?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It's Mine! The rims are OZ Monte Carlo with Carbon Fiber Centers 16 X 7 1/2 offset 5 3/8 inch, Part Number 23032202. Car is lowered 1 1/2 inch front and rear.<BR> [[/B][/QUOTE]<P>Unfortunatley OZ no longer makes those wheels , I contacted there US distributor when I wanted a set... No longer in production<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
