Z||000017||MD_Fiero||08-09-2001||10:12 PM||||californiakid...where did you get the tail covers??...also...a question for all these guys with big engines...3.5 liters..etc....<P><BR>what do you do with the front end?...being so light, and that the engine is in the rear..doesnt air ever get underneath and lift the car up some?..thanks!<P><BR>im trying to decide...i might sell the 2m4 for a GT...and go for a new engine..etc...||||reg||1
Z||000018||California Kid||08-09-2001||10:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MD_Fiero:<BR><B>californiakid...where did you get the tail covers??...also...a question for all these guys with big engines...3.5 liters..etc....<P><BR>what do you do with the front end?...being so light, and that the engine is in the rear..doesnt air ever get underneath and lift the car up some?..thanks!<P><BR>im trying to decide...i might sell the 2m4 for a GT...and go for a new engine..etc...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't know what you mean by "tail covers", but side scoops were bought through FOCOA, tail lamps stock 88.<P>Front end isn't that light, weight distribution on my car is 55% Rear, 45% Front. Aluminum Head V8 only adds 100 lbs to vehicle weight and that includes the 4 Core Radiator (with fluid) up front. On acceleration the front end stays planted, almost lifts front tires on launch. At speed the car stays planted to the highway, doesn't get loose (very stable at 165) at high speed like the Vettes or IROC Camaros'. This is due mainly to the design of the front fascia and the front and rear being lowered 1 1/2 (allowing less air to get under the body). <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||MD_Fiero||08-10-2001||12:05 AM||||ok, thank you...what i meant by tail light covers is...to me the tails look black...didnt know they came that color stock..thanks||||reg||1
